# Development Standards

## Atomic Slices

Every change must be a small, self-contained unit. One concern per commit — don't mix feature work with refactors or unrelated fixes.

## Tests First (TDD)

1. Write a failing test that describes the expected behaviour.
2. Implement the minimum code to make it pass.
3. Refactor while keeping tests green.

## External Services Behind Interfaces

All external services (OpenAI, event providers, email, etc.) must be accessed through injectable interfaces. Production code depends on the interface; concrete implementations are injected at the composition root.

```typescript
// Define the contract
interface EventProvider {
  search(artist: string, location: Location): Promise<Event[]>;
}

// Inject via function parameter or constructor
function ingestEvents(provider: EventProvider, ...) { ... }
```

## Schema Changes Require Migration + Tests

- Every schema change goes through `drizzle-kit generate`.
- Each migration must have a corresponding test verifying the new state.
- No hand-written SQL outside of Drizzle migration files.

## No Real Network Calls in Tests

Use MSW to intercept HTTP requests. Tests must never hit real endpoints.
